text:
{
  "agreed_facts": [
    "For the quarter ended May 31, 2026, revenue increased 60% year over year to $8.222 million, net income increased 31% to $2.948 million, and EBITDA increased 29% to $4.685 million; both sides note these results match the supplied model rather than establish a forecast beat.",
    "Water and wastewater revenue rose 119% to $4.659 million, deliveries increased to 631 acre-feet from 76, and water taps sold increased to 66 from 40.",
    "Lot sales revenue increased 19% to $3.006 million. The company expects substantial completion of Phase 2D by fiscal 2026 year-end and approximately 159 Phase 2E lots in fiscal 2027, paced to builder absorption.",
    "Cash and cash equivalents declined to $8.440 million from $21.931 million. The supplied evidence does not establish the cash-flow outlook or funding needs.",
    "The supplied evidence does not test whether demand and timing kill criteria have been triggered, and does not establish the durability of the quarter's growth."
  ],
  "open_disagreements": [
    {
      "topic": "Whether the sharp increase in water activity indicates durable, broad-based demand or an unproven mix of demand sources",
      "bull": "Higher water and wastewater revenue, deliveries, and tap sales support growth in both water demand and housing-related activity.",
      "bear": "The figures do not quantify oil-and-gas's contribution or show that either source of demand will persist; the increase could be temporary or concentrated.",
      "what_would_resolve": "The company's Form 10-Q for the quarter ended May 31, 2026, including segment and MD&A disclosures that separate oil-and-gas water sales from development-related water and tap revenue, followed by comparable disclosures in subsequent quarterly Forms 10-Q."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Whether the cash decline signals meaningful funding risk as development proceeds",
      "bull": "Cash declined materially, but the supplied balance alone does not establish a funding shortfall; the bull treats it as a reason for caution rather than a forecast.",
      "bear": "The decline warrants scrutiny of potential funding needs during Phase 2E construction.",
      "what_would_resolve": "The May 31, 2026 Form 10-Q cash-flow statement and liquidity, capital-resources, and commitments disclosures, plus subsequent filings showing cash flows, construction spending, and any new borrowing or equity financing."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Whether Phase 2D and Phase 2E execution is on schedule relative to prior guidance",
      "bull": "Current plans remain constructive: Phase 2D is expected to be substantially complete by fiscal year-end, and Phase 2E lots are to be paced to builder absorption.",
      "bear": "Current guidance alone does not show whether timing has slipped or whether absorption will support the planned pace.",
      "what_would_resolve": "The prior company earnings release or investor presentation stating the earlier Phase 2D and Phase 2E schedules, compared with the May 31, 2026 Form 10-Q and the next company earnings release for updated milestones and lot-delivery plans."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Whether lot and tap activity confirms sustained builder absorption or satisfies the stated demand kill test",
      "bull": "Year-over-year growth in lot sales and taps is directionally supportive of conversion and absorption.",
      "bear": "One quarter does not establish a sustained trend or resolve the criterion requiring two consecutive quarters of stalled taps alongside a greater-than-25% decline in county single-family permits.",
      "what_would_resolve": "The next two quarterly company filings or earnings releases reporting comparable tap sales, together with the Arapahoe County single-family building-permit dataset for the corresponding year-over-year periods."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The parties agree that reported results and water and tap activity grew year over year, while cash declined and the supplied figures do not establish a forecast beat or durable trend. They differ mainly in how much weight to give the operating growth versus unresolved questions about demand mix, execution, and funding; the specified filings and permit data can address those questions."
}
